# What never belongs in the image.
#
# An allow-list would be safer and this is not one, deliberately: the Dockerfile
# copies named directories rather than `.`, so this file is the second line
# rather than the only one. It exists so the build context stays small and so a
# stray local artifact cannot ride along if that ever changes.

.git
.github
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# The local database and anything else the app wrote. A deployment gets an empty
# one and a volume; a workstation's rack is not a fixture.
data/

# Tests, harnesses and the executable documentation. They run in CI against the
# source, not against the image, and the image is not where anybody runs them.
tests/
walkthrough/
governance/
vendor/
docs/

# Notes, records and review packets. None of it is served.
*.md
!README.md

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
